#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:1
msgid "Release 2.30.0 (2025-07-07)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:3
msgid "Backward-incompatible changes and deprecations"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:5
msgid ""
"[`build-dir`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-build-dir) no longer defaults "
"to `$TMPDIR`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:7
msgid ""
"The directory in which temporary build directories are created no longer "
"defaults to `TMPDIR` or `/tmp`, to avoid builders making their directories "
"world-accessible. This behavior allowed escaping the build sandbox and can "
"cause build impurities even when not used maliciously. We now default to "
"`builds` in `NIX_STATE_DIR` (which is `/nix/var/nix/builds` in the default "
"configuration)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:13
msgid ""
"Deprecate manually making structured attrs using the `__json` attribute "
"[\\#13220](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13220)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:15
msgid ""
"The proper way to create a derivation using [structured attrs](../language/"
"advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-structuredAttrs) in the Nix language is by "
"using `__structuredAttrs = true` with [`builtins.derivation`](../language/"
"builtins.html#builtins-derivation). However, by exploiting how structured "
"attrs are implemented, it has also been possible to create them by setting "
"the `__json` environment variable to a serialized JSON string. This sneaky "
"alternative method is now deprecated, and may be disallowed in future "
"versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:22
msgid ""
"Rename `nix profile install` to [`nix profile add`](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-profile-add.md) [\\#13224](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13224)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:24
msgid ""
"The command `nix profile install` has been renamed to [`nix profile add`](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-add.md) (though the former is still "
"available as an alias). This is because the verb \"add\" is a better antonym "
"for the verb \"remove\" (i.e. `nix profile remove`). Nix also does not have "
"install hooks or general behavior often associated with \"installing\"."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:26
msgid "Performance improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:28
msgid "This release has a number performance improvements, in particular:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:30
msgid ""
"Reduce the size of value from 24 to 16 bytes [\\#13407](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/13407)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:32
msgid ""
"This shaves off a very significant amount of memory used for evaluation "
"(~20% percent reduction in maximum heap size and ~17% in total bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:34
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:36
msgid ""
"Add [stack sampling evaluation profiler](../advanced-topics/eval-"
"profiler.md) [\\#13220](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13220)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:38
msgid ""
"The Nix evaluator now supports [stack sampling evaluation profiling](../"
"advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md) via the [`--eval-profiler flamegraph`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-profiler) setting. It outputs collapsed "
"call stack information to the file specified by [`--eval-profile-file`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-profile-file) (`nix.profile` by default) "
"in a format directly consumable by `flamegraph.pl` and compatible tools like "
"[speedscope](https://speedscope.app/). Sampling frequency can be configured "
"via [`--eval-profiler-frequency`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-"
"profiler-frequency) (99 Hz by default)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:44
msgid ""
"Unlike the existing [`--trace-function-calls`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-trace-function-calls), this profiler includes the name of the "
"function being called when it's available."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:47
msgid ""
"[`nix repl`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-repl.md) prints which variables "
"were loaded [\\#11406](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11406)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:49
msgid ""
"Instead of `Added <n> variables` it now prints the first 10 variables that "
"were added to the global scope."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:51
msgid ""
"`nix flake archive`: Add [`--no-check-sigs`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"flake-archive.md#opt-no-check-sigs) option [\\#13277](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/13277)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:53
msgid ""
"This is useful when using [`nix flake archive`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"flake-archive.md) with the destination set to a remote store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:55
msgid ""
"Emit warnings for IFDs with [`trace-import-from-derivation`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-trace-import-from-derivation) option [\\#13279](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13279)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:57
msgid ""
"While we have the setting [`allow-import-from-derivation`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-allow-import-from-derivation) to deny import-from-"
"derivation (IFD), sometimes users would like to observe IFDs during CI "
"processes to gradually phase out the idiom. The new setting `trace-import-"
"from-derivation`, when set, logs a simple warning to the console."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:59
msgid ""
"`json-log-path` setting [\\#13003](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13003)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:61
msgid ""
"New setting [`json-log-path`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-json-log-"
"path) that sends a copy of all Nix log messages (in JSON format) to a file "
"or Unix domain socket."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:63
msgid ""
"Non-flake inputs now contain a `sourceInfo` attribute [\\#13164](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13164) [\\#13170](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/13170)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:65
msgid ""
"Flakes have always had a `sourceInfo` attribute which describes the source "
"of the flake. The `sourceInfo.outPath` is often identical to the flake's "
"`outPath`. However, it can differ when the flake is located in a "
"subdirectory of its source."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:68
msgid ""
"Non-flake inputs (i.e. inputs with [`flake = false`](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-flake.md?highlight=false#flake-inputs)) can also be located at some "
"path _within_ a wider source. This usually happens when defining a relative "
"path input within the same source as the parent flake, e.g. `inputs.foo.url "
"= ./some-file.nix`. Such relative inputs will now inherit their parent's "
"`sourceInfo`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:72
msgid ""
"This also means it is now possible to use `?dir=subdir` on non-flake inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:74
msgid ""
"This iterates on the work done in 2.26 to improve relative path support "
"([\\#10089](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10089)), and resolves a "
"regression introduced in 2.28 relating to nested relative path inputs "
"([\\#13164](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13164))."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:77
msgid "Miscellaneous changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:79
msgid ""
"[`builtins.sort`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-sort) uses PeekSort "
"[\\#12623](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12623)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:81
msgid ""
"Previously it used libstdc++'s `std::stable_sort()`. However, that "
"implementation is not reliable if the user-supplied comparison function is "
"not a strict weak ordering."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:83
msgid ""
"Revert incomplete closure mixed download and build feature [\\#77](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/77) [\\#12628](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/12628) [\\#13176](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13176)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:85
msgid ""
"Since Nix 1.3 ([commit `299141e`](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"299141ecbd08bae17013226dbeae71e842b4fdd7) in 2013) Nix has attempted to mix "
"together upstream fresh builds and downstream substitutions when remote "
"substuters contain an \"incomplete closure\" (have some store objects, but "
"not the store objects they reference). This feature is now removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:88
msgid ""
"In the worst case, removing this feature could cause more building "
"downstream, but it should not cause outright failures, since this is not "
"happening for opaque store objects that we don't know how to build if we "
"decide not to substitute. In practice, however, we doubt even more building "
"is very likely to happen. Remote stores that are missing dependencies in "
"arbitrary ways (e.g. corruption) don't seem to be very common."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:92
msgid ""
"On the contrary, when remote stores fail to implement the [closure property]"
"(../store/store-object.md#closure-property), it is usually an _intentional_ "
"choice on the part of the remote store, because it wishes to serve as an "
"\"overlay\" store over another store, such as `https://cache.nixos.org`. If "
"an \"incomplete closure\" is encountered in that situation, the right fix is "
"not to do some sort of \"franken-building\" as this feature implemented, but "
"instead to make sure both substituters are enabled in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.30.md:95
msgid ""
"(In the future, we should make it easier for remote stores to indicate this "
"to clients, to catch settings that won't work in general before a missing "
"dependency is actually encountered.)"
msgstr ""

